course: dictionary
lesson: 5188
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear many coats. The word jack can be a tool, a playing card, a plug socket, a game, a flag, a name, or a verb. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it, because they are the context.
explain: Ruby is waiting at a wet bus stop, and her brother says, «Oh brilliant, best day ever». Jack is a person speaking, so here jack is a name. The clue is that he is Ruby's brother.
explain: «You must never go under a car held up only by a jack, because it can slip.» A car is heavy, and something that holds it up must be a tool. Swap in your meaning: a tool that lifts a car still makes sense, so that is the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have many meanings, so always check the clues before you decide.
fact: A car jack is a tool for lifting a heavy thing, like a car, a little way off the ground.
fact: «Jack» can be a boy's name, often a nickname for John, and in fairy tales Jack is a brave, clever boy, as in «Jack and the Beanstalk».
fact: «Jack it in» means give up, and «jack up» means lift with a jack or raise prices.
exercise: «You must never go under a car held up only by a jack, because it can slip.» What is a jack here? | *A tool for lifting a heavy thing a little way off the ground | A socket where you plug in a lead | A playing card with a young man on it | A small flag on a ship
exercise: In a pack of cards, which card sits between the ten and the queen? | An ace | A king | *A jack | A joker
exercise: «Oh brilliant, best day ever», says her brother Jack. What is Jack here? | A game with small metal pieces | *A boy's name, often short for John | A male donkey | A tool for lifting cars
test: In the game of jacks, what do you do? | *Pick up small metal pieces while bouncing a ball | Lift a heavy thing with a tool | Drive a car | Fly a small flag on a ship
test: In the saying «jack of all trades», what does jack mean? | *A person who can do many jobs | A card with a young man on it | A plug socket for a headphone | A tool for lifting things
exam: Ruby says, «I'm going to jack it in, this game is boring.» What does jack it in mean? | Steal it | *Give up | Lift it with a tool | Plug it in
